Good catch — this is exactly the "management plane vs. data plane" split that trips up almost everyone on Azure. Short answer: Contributor is not enough for Storage or ACR, but it is enough for Batch and Container Apps.

Why
Azure has two separate permission systems layered on the same resource:

Layer	What it covers	Is it in Contributor?
Actions (control/management plane)	Create, configure, delete the resource itself — e.g. create a storage account, change its SKU, create/resize a Batch pool, deploy a Container Apps revision	✅ Yes — Contributor grants Actions: "*"
DataActions (data plane)	Touch the data inside the resource — e.g. read/write an actual blob's bytes, docker push/pull an image	❌ No — Contributor's DataActions list is empty by design
Blob storage and Container Registry both split their permissions this way specifically so that "can manage the account" and "can touch the data in it" are separate, revocable grants. Batch and Container Apps don't have this split — their task/job/revision operations are ordinary Actions, not DataActions.

So concretely, with only Contributor:

You can do	You cannot do
Create/delete/configure the storage account, ACR, Batch account, ACA app as resources	Upload/download/list blobs (needs Storage Blob Data Contributor)
Create/resize Batch pools, create jobs, submit/cancel Batch tasks	docker push/docker pull to ACR (needs AcrPush/AcrPull)
Deploy ACA revisions, update env vars	Assign roles to anyone, including yourself (Microsoft.Authorization/roleAssignments/write is explicitly excluded from Contributor)
That last row matters too: if you only have Contributor, you also can't grant yourself Storage Blob Data Contributor or AcrPush — that requires Owner or User Access Administrator, which you probably don't have. So the fix isn't "use Contributor differently," it's asking the admin to add the two missing role assignments specifically:

Storage Blob Data Contributor on the storage account
AcrPush on the ACR (you'll need this in Phase 4 too, before you even get to Batch)
Everything else in your plan (Batch pool/job/task management, ACA deploys) will work fine on Contributor alone once you get there — it was only Storage and ACR that needed the extra data-plane roles.

